    "title": "Unconstitutional: Pleas Against Bihar Voter List Revision in Top Court",
    "text": "• Lok Sabha MP Mahua Moitra is one of the petitioners against the Special Intensive Revision (SIR) exercise.\n• The SIR exercise requires electors in Bihar to prove their eligibility again.\n• Bihar assembly elections are scheduled for October-November 2025.\n• Opposition leaders, including Rahul Gandhi and Tejashwi Yadav, have criticized the revision process.\n• They allege that the revision is an attempt to rig the elections in favor of the BJP and NDA.\n• The High Court dismissed a plea seeking the repeal of certain sections of the Bihar Nagrik Suraksha Act.\n• The court stated that issuing such a direction would amount to legislating, which is beyond its jurisdiction.",
